## How to run

### Option A — Locally (or in a Codespace)
```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd AAI2025-ML-Assignment
pip install -r requirements.txt
python ML/house_price_prediction.py
python ML/customer_churn_prediction.py
python ML/customer_segmentation.py
python ML/forecasting_sales.py
```

### Option B — Google Colab
1. Go to [colab.research.google.com](https://colab.research.google.com) → **File → Open notebook → GitHub tab**, paste your repo URL once it's pushed (see below), or just copy-paste one script's contents into a Colab cell.
2. Run the cell. Colab has full internet access, so the scripts will pull the **real** datasets automatically (you should see "Loaded ### REAL ..." printed, not the fallback message).
3. For the plots (`elbow_plot.png`, `demand_forecast.png`), add this to display them inline after the script's `plt.savefig(...)` line:
   ```python
   from IPython.display import Image, display
   display(Image("elbow_plot.png"))
   ```

## Outputs produced

- `ML/customer_segments.csv` — cluster assignment for every customer (Part 3)
