- `ML/demand_forecast.png` — historical vs. forecasted housing demand (Extra Credit)
- Console output for every script prints the trained model's coefficients, evaluation metrics (R², MAE, accuracy, ROC AUC — added beyond what the starter code checked), and predictions, as required by the assignment.

## Submitting via GitHub

From inside this folder:
```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Complete AAI2025 ML homework: house prices, churn, segmentation, forecasting"
```
Then create an empty repo on github.com (no README/gitignore, so it doesn't
conflict with what you already have), and push:
```bash
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/<repo-name>.git
git push -u origin main
```
Submit the resulting `https://github.com/<your-username>/<repo-name>` link
in Canvas.

